== library | AFTERNOON · RESEARCH LIBRARY | quiet research library with computers, journals and soft light | cafe +laptop
ade (worried): Quddus, I googled fully funded PhD and got ten blogs, three scams, and one recipe for jollof.
quddus (talk): You need to search where real positions are posted. In many countries, a PhD is advertised like a job, with a salary.
ade (shock): A PhD with a salary?
quddus (thumbs): In places like Europe, many PhD positions are paid. You find them on job boards.
> 1f50e | WHERE TO LOOK | 1f30d EURAXESS (Europe research jobs) | 1f3db University PhD and job pages | 1f4da FindAPhD and similar boards | 1f52c Professors' lab websites

== office | NEXT DAY · STUDY ROOM | modern study room with a laptop, a calendar and coffee | desk @ade
ade (type): What do I search?
quddus (point): Use words like PhD position, doctoral researcher, or PhD studentship, plus your field. And set up email alerts.
ade (think): And then?
quddus (talk): Read the requirements carefully. Most want a CV, a motivation letter, and references. Apply to each one properly.
ade (cheer): Alerts set. Funded PhD, I'm coming. Jollof recipe, saved for later!
